    "question": "Does transferring complete internal post-training weight updates retain reasoning information discarded by the earlier bounded-rank projection, while keeping one native recurrent decoder?",
    "training": "Select the largest registered mix of the two pinned sibling decoders whose raw NLL stays within 0.045 of untouched Base on 36 independent train-only calibration passages. Mix all floating tensors in all 24 decoder layers, including norms, hybrid recurrence and attention. Preserve the Base token embedding, tied vocabulary head and final norm. Initialize fresh rank-eight LoRA on all layers and a stabilized shared second pass. Optimize 128 AdamW updates on three distinct publisher math solutions, one annotated reading answer and one raw prose passage per update. No separate donor executes at inference. The original qualified adapter and matched dense control are identity witnesses only. Archive the actual merged source identity.",
    "decision": "Failure to qualify a nonzero mixture stops training and testing. One preregistered fresh 32-item pair. Identical thinking prompt IDs, order, greedy 1024-token cap, scorer and measured time. Require >=2 net correct overall, strictly positive in both sources, no short-prefix loss in either source, candidate generation <=Base and full independent V3 language NLL <=Base+0.03. Blindly audit rejected completed answers and require positive mathematical content before replication. Stop on native resource guards. A failure closes this checkpoint; a pass permits independent replication, general reading, causal attribution and full 128K verification.",
